    "result_text": "Full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an `initials` field computed as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nFollowing the existing `displayName` pattern, I made two focused changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema, so `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(initials(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a small `initials(Owner)` default method that returns `Character.toUpperCase(first)+\".\"+Character.toUpperCase(last)+\".\"`.\n\nThe logic lives beside the analogous `displayName` derivation in the mapper (the natural home for name-formatting), keeping each method single-purpose. The `AcceptanceTest#coreComputesInitials` test and the rest of the suite pass.",
